# Tutorial 15 — UI Layout and Theme
# Dialogue box layout, menu screen files, style properties, and the config file structure.

@scenario {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_tutorial_15_ui_layout
@include {{CHARACTERS_INCLUDE}}
{{BG_DECL}}@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[set ui.textBoxAsset none]
[set ui.continueIndicator spinning_arrow]
[if tutorial_still]
[set ui.reduceMotion true]
[else]
[set ui.reduceMotion false]
[endif]
[if !tutorial_initialized]
[set tutorial_count 0]
[flag tutorial_initialized]
[endif]
[set ui.characterHeightFactor 1.5]
[set ui.characterBaselineY 1.5]
[set character.lavender.imageEffect none]
{{BG_START}}
[textspeed 28]
[autodelay 1650]
[show lavender center happy]
[wait 200]
Lavender: The text box you're reading right now, the name label above it, the choice buttons — all configurable through layout and style files.
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: This tutorial covers the config file structure for dialogue and menus.

@label lesson_menu
[show lavender far_left talking]
> Dialogue box — layout properties -> section_dialogue_box
> Menu screens — the three-file system -> section_menus
> Style properties — colors and fonts -> section_styles
> Layout properties — positioning values -> section_layout_files
> The menu registry -> section_registry
> Quick reference: UI files -> quick_reference
> Practice: design by genre -> practice_scene
> Back to Tutorial Hub -> return_hub

# ─── Quick Reference ─────────────────────────────────────────────

@label quick_reference
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: UI customization lives in config files:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}config/ui/dialogue.layout{/color} — text box position and size.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}config/ui/dialogue.style{/color} — dialogue colors and fonts.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}config/menu/menus/main.menu{/color} — items and actions.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}config/menu/layouts/default.layout{/color} — menu placement.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}config/menu/styles/default.style{/color} — menu appearance.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Checklist: edit one file type at a time, test at multiple resolutions, and keep readable contrast.
> Start the lesson sections -> section_dialogue_box
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Dialogue Box ────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label section_dialogue_box
[show lavender left talking]
Lavender: The dialogue box is configured in {b}config/ui/dialogue.layout{/b}. Key properties:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}textBoxX = 0.10{/color} — horizontal position (0 = left edge, 1 = right edge).
narrator: {color=#8888cc}textBoxY = 0.72{/color} — vertical position (0 = top, 1 = bottom).
narrator: {color=#8888cc}textBoxWidth = 0.80{/color} — width as fraction of screen.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}textBoxHeight = 0.22{/color} — height as fraction of screen.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}textBoxOpacity = 0.75{/color} — background transparency (0 = invisible, 1 = solid).
narrator: {color=#8888cc}textBoxAsset = assets/ui/textbox.png{/color} — custom background image (optional).
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: The style file {b}config/ui/dialogue.style{/b} controls appearance:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}textColor = #ffffff{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}nameTextColor = #aaddff{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}fontFamily = Noto Sans{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}fontSize = 22{/color}
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Edit these files directly, or use the visual editor: drag the text box, change colors, see updates live.
> Next: menu screens -> section_menus
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Menu Screens ────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label section_menus
[show lavender right talking]
Lavender: Each menu screen (title, save, load, settings) uses three files:
narrator: {b}Screen definition:{/b} {color=#8888cc}config/menu/screens/main.menu{/color}
narrator: Declares menu items, their labels, and their actions (new_game, load, settings, quit).
narrator: {b}Layout:{/b} {color=#8888cc}config/menu/layouts/main.layout{/color}
narrator: Where items appear — list position, line height, text alignment.
narrator: {b}Style:{/b} {color=#8888cc}config/menu/styles/main.style{/color}
narrator: How items look — colors, fonts, selected/disabled states, button assets.
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: The screen file references its layout and style by ID. Change the style → different look, same positions. Change the layout → items move, colors stay.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: This separation lets an artist tweak colors while a designer repositions elements — independently.
> Next: style properties -> section_styles
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Style Properties ───────────────────────────────────────────

@label section_styles
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Style files are key-value properties. Menu style properties:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}itemColor = #cccccc{/color} — default text color.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}itemSelectedColor = #ffffff{/color} — hovered or selected.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}itemDisabledColor = #555555{/color} — grayed-out items.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}fontFamily = Noto Sans{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}fontSize = 28{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}fontWeight = NORMAL{/color}
[show lavender left talking]
Lavender: Dialogue style adds:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}choiceBgColor = #333333{/color} — choice button background.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}choiceTextColor = #ffffff{/color} — choice button text.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}choiceSelectedBgColor = #4a6eaa{/color} — highlighted choice.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}nameBoxOpacity = 0.8{/color}
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Design rule: use 2–3 colors max. Derive selected, disabled, and hover variants from the same base hue.
> Next: layout properties -> section_layout_files
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Layout Properties ──────────────────────────────────────────

@label section_layout_files
[show lavender right talking]
Lavender: Layout files control positioning. Menu layout example:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}listYStart = 0.35{/color} — vertical start of the item list (normalized).
narrator: {color=#8888cc}lineHeight = 50.0{/color} — pixels between items.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}listWidthFactor = 0.56{/color} — width of the list area as screen fraction.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}textAlign = center{/color} — left, center, or right.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}titleY = 0.12{/color} — title position.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}hintsBottomMargin = 0.07{/color} — hint text margin from bottom.
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Values are either {b}normalized (0–1){/b} for positions or {b}pixel-based{/b} for sizes.
Lavender: You can edit these directly for precision, or use the visual editor for drag-and-drop adjustment.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Raw files are version-controllable and diffable. Visual editors are faster for iteration. Use both.
> Next: registry -> section_registry
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Menu Registry ──────────────────────────────────────────────

@label section_registry
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: The {b}menu registry{/b} ties everything together:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}config/menu/registry/menu.registry{/color}
narrator: It declares which menus exist, which is the default, and which layouts/styles they use:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}defaultMenu = main{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}menus = main, save, load, settings{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}layouts = main, save, load, settings{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}styles = main, save, load, settings{/color}
[show lavender left talking]
Lavender: When you add a new menu screen, register it here. If a menu isn't in the registry, the engine won't load it.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Four files per menu: .menu (definition), .layout (positioning), .style (appearance), plus the registry entry.
> Practice: design by genre -> practice_scene
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Practice ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label practice_scene
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Different genres need different UI personalities. Pick one and I'll describe the properties to change.
> Horror game UI -> practice_horror
> Cozy/cheerful VN -> practice_cheerful
> Minimalist design -> practice_minimal

@label practice_horror
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Horror: the UI should feel like it's barely there.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}textBoxOpacity = 0.35{/color} — almost transparent. The scene dominates.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}textColor = #cccccc{/color} — muted, not bright white.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}itemSelectedColor = #882222{/color} — dark red accent.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}fontFamily = Crimson Text{/color} — serif, slightly formal.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}choiceBgColor = #1a1a1a{/color} — nearly invisible buttons.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: The player should feel uneasy even reading the menu. The UI lurks instead of announcing itself.
[jump practice_done]

@label practice_cheerful
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Cozy: warm, readable, inviting.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}textBoxOpacity = 0.85{/color} — high opacity for comfort.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}textColor = #3a2a1a{/color} — dark brown on cream.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}itemColor = #6b4226{/color} — warm earth tones.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}itemSelectedColor = #ff9944{/color} — bright orange highlight.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}fontFamily = Quicksand{/color} — rounded, friendly.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}choiceBgColor = #fff3e0{/color} — soft cream buttons.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: The UI should make the player smile before they read a word. Warmth and readability together.
[jump practice_done]

@label practice_minimal
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Minimal: clean, typographic, nothing extra.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}textBoxOpacity = 0.60{/color} — present but unobtrusive.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}textColor = #e0e0e0{/color} — off-white.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}itemColor = #aaaaaa{/color} — soft gray.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}itemSelectedColor = #ffffff{/color} — pure white selected.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}fontFamily = Inter{/color} — clean sans-serif.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}lineHeight = 60.0{/color} — generous spacing.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}textBoxAsset ={/color} — no background image. Solid color only.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Minimalism works when every remaining element earns its place. Nothing decorative, everything functional.
[jump practice_done]

@label practice_done
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Copy any of these property sets into your style and layout files to start from a genre-appropriate base.
Lavender: Test with live dialogue and real menu density — mockups are always more forgiving than the real thing.
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_15]
[flag tutorial_done_15]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[goto {{HUB_TARGET}}:topics_page_3]
